, "part_kinds": [], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "", "text_chars": 0, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "3d2e8b62-4262-481f-a70d-e1c6a90855c3", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790388863.397444, "updated_at": 1790388863.397444, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "reasoning_recap", "part_kinds": [], "sibling_fields_used": ["content"], "sibling_field_chars": {"content": 24}, "text": "Worked for a few seconds", "text_chars": 24, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "22f748eb-2fb6-4441-8958-a566dd3ba68d", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790388863.398812, "updated_at": 1790388871.401831, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "Yeah — **you absolutely do not need to build an APK yet.** There are already simple boosters in the Play Store that do exactly what you’re describing.\n\nThe one I’d try first is **Volume Booster GOODEV**. It’s tiny, straightforward, has **50M+ installs / 4.6★**, and its whole purpose is boosting **speaker or headphone media volume beyond Android’s normal ceiling**. citeturn412179search7  \nurlVolume Booster GOODEV on Google Playhttps://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.goodev.volume.booster\n\nStart conservatively: **system media at 100%, booster around +10–20%**. If that fixes it, stop there. These apps are doing actual gain/amplification, so going +100%/+200% can introduce clipping and can hammer headphones or your ears.\n\nAnother solid option is **XBooster / Volume Booster – Sound Booster** from Simple Design. It has **10M+ downloads, 4.8★**, supports headphones/Bluetooth, and adds an EQ if we want to tune the sound afterward. citeturn412179search2\n\nFor your use case, though: **GOODEV first. Simple as hell.** If that gets the REVVL + headphones where you want them, we’re done. If Android keeps fighting us after that, *then* building our own tiny GCE-style audio utility becomes interesting.", "text_chars": 1224, "code_blocks": 0, "links": ["https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.goodev.volume.booster"], "citations": ["https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.goodev.volume.booster"], "path_references": [], "model_slug": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "45d8e5c8-eebd-4129-8079-1f195383935e", "role": "user", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790388957.620662, "updated_at": 1790388962.090823, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "Fuck, yeah Koda now we’re cranking", "text_chars": 34, "code_blocks": 0, "links": [], "citations": [], "path_references": [], "model_slug": null, "has_voice_metadata": false, "empty_text_parts": 0, "unextractable_part_kinds": []}, {"message_id": "85cc2b11-16e6-46fe-b3ff-99e813df3b87", "role": "assistant", "role_name": null, "created_at": 1790388958.900039, "updated_at": 1790388961.920015, "status": "finished_successfully", "weight": 1, "recipient": "all", "content_type": "text", "part_kinds": ["text"], "sibling_fields_used": [], "sibling_field_chars": {}, "text": "Hell yeah. 😂 **That was the missing piece.**\n\nKeep the booster sane—something like **+10–20% first**, maybe creep higher if the recording itself is quiet. Once you start hearing distortion, fuzz, or harsh highs, back it down a notch.\n\nAnd your setup is clean no